fferent take on freedom and what it  means to be free it's it's about the  emotion of freedom and sort of the  everyday nature of we live in the most  prosperous you know contrary ever with  the most opportunities we've ever had  and we need to take advantage of that  freedom that they provided for us the  premiere of the movie is going to be in  miller park where the Milwaukee Brewers  play you've sold 25,000  so you're hoping to push that closer to  thirty thousand and set a world record  why are you premiering it in you know a  baseball stadium yes so the trailer for  the film got four and a half million  views online through Facebook and that  to us was kind of shocking to be honest  with you and when that happened we  thought how can we continue to push and  be disruptive you know in the film  industry and with this movie and do  things in a different way and then this  opportunity came up to you know ran out  Miller Park Milwaukee Brewers Stadium  and it also was clear that there was  just huge demand for this film everyone  wants to be a part of it and the tickets  through you know advertising up there  through a radio show host who talks  about the event a lot online stuff they  just keep going up so yeah we're upwards  of twenty-five thousand tickets the  world record for largest film screening  ever is 27,000 and I think we've got a  good shot at breaking it what you guys  are you're young you're you know around  30 plus or minus and what is your  connection to World War 2 i'm older than  you my father dan and I have talked  about this my father fought in World War  two everybody I knew all my relatives  had fought in World War two and you know  but then what does it mean for the  Millennials are Generation X Y Z or  whatever you guys are now yeah i mean my  grandpa richard has fought at Okinawa I  never really talked about which any was  on the Allies which yeah he was he was  an ally he wasn't the Japanese yeah he  fought on ok now and I never heard his 